  "binding": "Boots a headless fixture with one Simulation screen showing the light-gun cartridge (src/Puck.World/Assets/cartridges/light-gun.cgb.puck), whose picture is lit on the left half and dark on the right and whose one rule publishes the $light operand into its first variable every frame; a read binding mirrors that byte into the world's seen slot. The seat engages the screen and types source.pointer.origin and source.pointer.direction once per phase, since a typed ray is held until it is aimed again or cleared. Aimed at the lit half, the held aim still reaches the gun two ticks later, screen.state echoes it on the picture's left quarter, and the cartridge publishes seen=1; aimed once at the dark half the gun moves right and seen falls to 0; after source.pointer.clear the gun is off. The recorded run replays exactly. The discriminating leg aims once at the dark half and holds it throughout: the gun is on the picture's right, and seen never reads 1.",
